<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<section xml:id="schedule">
  <title>Fall 2026 Calendar and Important Dates</title>

  <p>
    <xref ref="table-calendar"/> lists the key dates for Fall 2026. Week 1
    begins on Monday, September 21. The three midterm exams and the final exam
    are labeled <q>Exam</q> in the table.
  </p>

  <table xml:id="table-calendar">
    <title>Fall 2026 week-by-week calendar</title>
    <tabular halign="left" top="minor" bottom="minor">
      <col width="12%"/>
      <col width="24%"/>
      <col width="64%"/>
      <row header="yes" bottom="minor">
        <cell>Week</cell>
        <cell>Dates</cell>
        <cell>Event</cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>1</cell>
        <cell>Sep 21 <ndash/> 25</cell>
        <cell>Monday, Sep 21 <mdash/> classes begin</cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>2</cell>
        <cell>Sep 28 <ndash/> Oct 2</cell>
        <cell></cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>3</cell>
        <cell>Oct 5 <ndash/> 9</cell>
        <cell>Friday, Oct 9 <mdash/> <alert>Exam #1</alert></cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>4</cell>
        <cell>Oct 12 <ndash/> 16</cell>
        <cell>Monday, Oct 12 <mdash/> Indigenous Peoples' Day; academic holiday, no class</cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>5</cell>
        <cell>Oct 19 <ndash/> 23</cell>
        <cell>Monday, Oct 19 <mdash/> last day to drop classes without a W, by 5 PM</cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>6</cell>
        <cell>Oct 26 <ndash/> 30</cell>
        <cell>Friday, Oct 30 <mdash/> <alert>Exam #2</alert></cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>7</cell>
        <cell>Nov 2 <ndash/> 6</cell>
        <cell></cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>8</cell>
        <cell>Nov 9 <ndash/> 13</cell>
        <cell>Monday, Nov 9 <mdash/> last day to drop classes with a W, by 5 PM</cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>9</cell>
        <cell>Nov 16 <ndash/> 20</cell>
        <cell>Friday, Nov 20 <mdash/> <alert>Exam #3</alert></cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell><mdash/></cell>
        <cell>Nov 23 <ndash/> 27</cell>
        <cell>Academic holiday, Thanksgiving week <mdash/> no classes</cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>10</cell>
        <cell>Nov 30 <ndash/> Dec 4</cell>
        <cell>Friday, Dec 4 <mdash/> classes end</cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>Finals</cell>
        <cell>Dec 7 <ndash/> 11</cell>
        <cell><alert>Final Exam</alert> <mdash/> scheduled by the Registrar's Office; see <xref ref="table-final-exam"/></cell>
      </row>
    </tabular>
  </table>

  <p>
    <alert>The date and time of the final exam are set by the Office of the
    Registrar, not by me.</alert> The University assigns every final exam
    slot from the class meeting time, and I have no say in it and cannot
    change it. <xref ref="table-final-exam"/> simply copies the entries for
    our two sections from the Registrar's
    <url href="https://www.scu.edu/registrar/undergraduate-final-exams-schedule/">Undergraduate Final Exams Schedule</url>.
    Please check the date, time, and room in your Workday course schedule:
    the Registrar's schedule takes precedence over this copy, and rooms can
    change.
  </p>

  <table xml:id="table-final-exam">
    <title>Final exam date and time, as scheduled by the Office of the Registrar</title>
    <tabular halign="left" top="minor" bottom="minor">
      <col width="22%"/>
      <col width="28%"/>
      <col width="50%"/>
      <row header="yes" bottom="minor">
        <cell>Section</cell>
        <cell>Class meets</cell>
        <cell>Final exam</cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>MATH 13-3</cell>
        <cell>M W F, 9:15 AM</cell>
        <cell>Wednesday, December 9, 9:10 AM <ndash/> 12:10 PM</cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>MATH 13-4</cell>
        <cell>M W F, 10:30 AM</cell>
        <cell>Friday, December 11, 9:10 AM <ndash/> 12:10 PM</cell>
      </row>
    </tabular>
  </table>

  <p>
    <em>Reminder:</em> assignments are due on Fridays at 11:59 PM, except in
    the exam weeks (weeks 3, 6, and 9), when they are due on Wednesday at
    11:59 PM. No late submissions will be accepted.
  </p>
</section>
